y a card higher than 8.\n\nReason: To prevent the landlord from winning immediately, I must play a card higher than ♠8. Since my teammate passed previously when they could have beaten ♠8, they likely cannot continue. Therefore, I am the only one who can stop the landlord now. I should use the smallest card necessary to beat ♠8 to conserve strength. Thus, I choose ♣9 over ♠K.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣9"]}'}
